      "name": "The Flat Rate Movers — Route 81 Corridor Operations Dataset",
      "description": "Route 81 corridor operations from The Flat Rate Movers — moving and logistics dispatch along Interstate 81, I-66 and I-70, run from two dispatch branches that sit on the corridor itself: Winchester, VA, where I-81 meets I-66, and Martinsburg, WV, on I-81 with the I-70 connection. Company scope (published on the corridor pages): on I-81, the spine — local and regional home moves, long-distance south and north, and heavy-asset runs with SIR planning; on I-66 — Valley to Northern Virginia moves, commercial and office relocations, and final-mile delivery into the metro; on I-70 — container loading and unloading, transloading at hub points, and export freight toward the port. Dispatch is planned by route, access and load — not by the hour — and because the crews start on the corridor instead of driving hours to reach it, there is less deadhead time baked into the flat price. Heavy-asset runs on the corridor are surveyed and floor-checked to L/360 under SIR Structural Integrity Relocation and the KIM-GS Protocol, like any SIR move. Every corridor job is quoted at one flat rate agreed in writing before move day — the guarantee: Guaranteed Flat Rate or Your Move is Free!",
